==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|pt}} {{m|pt|cridare|crīdāre|to cry out, publish, proclaim}} (compare Spanish {{m|es|gritar}}, Catalan {{m|ca|cridar}}, French {{m|fr|crier}}, Italian {{m|it|gridare}}), of uncertain origin. Perhaps from {{etyl|la|pt}} {{m|la|quiritare||to shriek, wail}} (per Diez), or from {{etyl|frk|pt}} {{m|frk|*kritan|*krītan|to cry out, scream, proclaim}} (per Littré), compare {{cog|dum|critan|crītan|to cry}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Portugal}} {{IPA|/ɡɾi.ˈtaɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{a|Portugal|following an oral sound}} {{IPA|[ɣɾi.ˈtaɾ]|lang=pt}}

