==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|osp|cridar|cridar, gridar|}}, from {{inh|es|ML.|crīdāre||to cry out, publish, proclaim}}, from {{der|es|frk||*krītan|}} "to cry out, scream, proclaim" (--Littré), related to {{cog|dum|critan|crītan|to cry}}.

An alternative (less likely) origin is {{etyl|la|es}} {{m|la|quirito||to shriek, hiss}}.

Cognate with {{cog|ca|cridar}}, {{cog|fr|crier}}, and {{cog|it|gridare}}), and {{cog|pt|gritar}}. Compare {{cog|en|cry}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡɾiˈtaɾ/|lang=es}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb|grit|ar}}

# to [[shout]], to [[scream]], to [[cry]] out, to [[call out]]
